From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:42:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(control): the profile's cursor shape reaches ghostty

Found by hand: a ghostty pane drew a block cursor beside a cascadia pane
drawing a bar. Not a configuration problem - cursorShape was simply never
forwarded, so ghostty used its own default and the profile's setting applied to
one pane out of two.

ghostty has four shapes to WT's six. Bar, Underscore, FilledBox and EmptyBox map
exactly; Vintage and DoubleUnderscore both become an underline, and the test
lists them as approximations rather than leaving that to be discovered. Vintage
is why CursorHeight is not forwarded either - ghostty has no height control for
an underline, so sending the height would imply an effect it cannot have.

This sets the default only. A program can still ask for another shape with
DECSCUSR on either engine, and ghostty's shell integration puts a bar at the
prompt regardless, so a profile's cursorShape is the starting point rather than
the last word.

WT suites: unitControl 62/62.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
---
 .../GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp             | 36 ++++++++++++++++
 .../GhosttySettingsTests.cpp                  | 41 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
index ce1b9199f..f17f9769d 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
@@ -106,6 +106,42 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         // clipboard - measured, because that was the regression to fear.
         set("selection-trim-line", "false");
 
+        // --- Cursor -------------------------------------------------------
+        // Found by hand: a ghostty pane drew a block where the cascadia pane
+        // beside it drew a bar, because the profile's cursorShape was never
+        // forwarded and ghostty used its own default.
+        //
+        // ghostty offers four shapes to WT's six. DoubleUnderscore and Vintage
+        // both become an underline - Vintage is a short underscore and ghostty
+        // has no height control for it, which is also why CursorHeight is not
+        // forwarded at all. Those two are the approximations; the other four
+        // are exact.
+        //
+        // Only the default is set here. A program can still ask for a different
+        // shape with DECSCUSR, on either engine, and ghostty's shell
+        // integration puts a bar at the prompt regardless - so a profile's
+        // cursorShape is the starting point rather than the last word.
+        if (const auto appearance = settings.try_as<Core::ICoreAppearance>())
+        {
+            switch (appearance.CursorShape())
+            {
+            case Core::CursorStyle::Bar:
+                set("cursor-style", "bar");
+                break;
+            case Core::CursorStyle::Underscore:
+            case Core::CursorStyle::DoubleUnderscore:
+            case Core::CursorStyle::Vintage:
+                set("cursor-style", "underline");
+                break;
+            case Core::CursorStyle::EmptyBox:
+                set("cursor-style", "block_hollow");
+                break;
+            case Core::CursorStyle::FilledBox:
+                set("cursor-style", "block");
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+
         // --- Padding ------------------------------------------------------
         // WT already insets the SwapChainPanel by this same padding, so asking
         // ghostty to pad as well would double it. Ours is therefore zero, and
diff --git a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
index d148aafa9..cd44a051d 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,8 @@ namespace ControlUnitTests
         TEST_METHOD(PaddingIsZeroBecauseWindowsTerminalAlreadyPads);
         TEST_METHOD(SchemeProducesForegroundBackgroundAndFullPalette);
         TEST_METHOD(WordDelimitersReachTheEngine);
-        TEST_METHOD(TripleClickHighlightsTheWholeLine);
